{"schema_version":"1.9.2","id":"USN-9017-1","published":"2026-11-10T06:01:57Z","modified":"2026-11-11T09:44:40.035134977Z","related":["UBUNTU-CVE-2026-120451","UBUNTU-CVE-2026-120452"],"upstream":["CVE-2026-120451","CVE-2026-120452","UBUNTU-CVE-2026-120451","UBUNTU-CVE-2026-120452"],"summary":"libgphoto2 vulnerabilities","details":"It was discovered that libgphoto2 did not properly manage memory when\ninitializing certain cameras. If a user were tricked into connecting a\nmalicious USB device, an attacker could possibly use this issue to cause\nlibgphoto2 to crash, resulting in a denial of service, or possibly execute\narbitrary code. (CVE-2026-120451)\n\nIt was discovered that libgphoto2 did not properly manage memory when\nprocessing certain thumbnails. If a user were tricked into connecting a\nmalicious USB device, an attacker could possibly use this issue to cause\nlibgphoto2 to crash, resulting in a denial of service, or expose sensitive\ninformation. (CVE-2026-120452)","affected":[{"package":{"name":"libgphoto2","ecosystem":"Ubuntu:Pro:14.04:LTS","purl":"pkg:deb/ubuntu/libgphoto2?arch=source&distro=esm-infra-legacy%2Ftrusty"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"2.5.3.1-1ubuntu2.2+esm1"}]}],"versions":["2.5.2-0ubuntu5","2.5.2-0ubuntu6","2.5.3.1-0ubuntu1","2.5.3.1-1ubuntu2","2.5.3.1-1ubuntu2.2"],"ecosystem_specific":{"availability":"Available with Ubuntu Pro with Legacy support add-on: https://ubuntu.com/pro","binaries":[{"binary_name":"libgphoto2-6","binary_version":"2.5.3.1-1ubuntu2.2+esm1"},{"binary_name":"libgphoto2-l10n","binary_version":"2.5.3.1-1ubuntu2.2+esm1"},{"binary_name":"libgphoto2-port10","binary_version":"2.5.3.1-1ubuntu2.2+esm1"}]},"database_specific":{"cves_map":{"cves":[{"id":"CVE-2026-120451","severity":[{"score":"CVSS:3.1/AV:P/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H","type":"CVSS_V3"},{"score":"CVSS:4.0/AV:P/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:H/VI:H/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N","type":"CVSS_V4"},{"score":"medium","type":"Ubuntu"}]},{"id"